# The repo is authored on Windows and runs on Linux: Vercel builds apps/web, and
# a VPS runs apps/worker under systemd. Normalising to LF in the index keeps a
# CRLF from reaching a place where it matters.
#
# The one that would actually bite: deploy/probe-worker.service. systemd
# tolerates CRLF in most fields but not all, and a unit that fails to parse on
# deploy day is a bad way to find out.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary-ish and generated files that must never be line-ending normalised.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.ico binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary

# The lockfile is generated. Marking it keeps it out of code review diffs.
pnpm-lock.yaml -diff linguist-generated=true

# .eml files are RFC 5322 and REQUIRE CRLF. None are committed today (outbox/ is
# ignored), but if a fixture ever is, normalising it would silently corrupt it.
*.eml -text
